{"step_index":1317,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:47:48Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-12T01:47:48+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-12T01:47:48+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/Challenge_e20263a9.lean`\nTotal Lines: 353\nTotal Bytes: 13918\nShowing lines 330 to 353\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n330:     have h0 := h_no0 v\n331:     omega\n332:   have h_sum : ∑ v : V, 1 ≤ ∑ v : V, (f v : ℕ) :=\n333:     Finset.sum_le_sum (fun v _ => h_ge1 v)\n334:   rw [Finset.sum_const, nsmul_eq_mul, mul_one] at h_sum\n335:   rw [Finset.card_univ] at h_sum\n336:   exact h_sum\n337: \n338: lemma mem_ballWithin_one_of_adj {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n339:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (c u : V) (hadj : G.Adj c u) :\n340:     u ∈ ballWithin G 1 c :=\n341:   mem_ballWithin_of_walk G (SimpleGraph.Walk.cons hadj SimpleGraph.Walk.nil)\n342: \n343: lemma mem_ballWithin_one_self {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n344:     (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (c : V) :\n345:     c ∈ ballWithin G 1 c :=\n346:   ballWithin_subset_succ G 0 c (Finset.mem_singleton_self c)\n347: \n348: theorem prove_e20263a9 : Candidate := by\n349:   sorry\n350: \n351: theorem refute_e20263a9 : ¬ Candidate := by\n352:   sorry\n353: \nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
{"step_index":1318,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:47:48Z","thinking":"**Examining lemma requirements**\n\nInitial focus is on the `Challenge_e20263a9.lean` file, specifically the lemmas available for use. The verified lemmas will be copied into this file. Starting with the first lemma: `ballWithin_one_eq_univ_of_adj_all`. This lemma seems useful.\n\n\n**Evaluating lemma applicability**\n\nConsidering the provided lemmas, `ballWithin_one_eq_univ_of_adj_all` seems directly relevant to establishing a small radius. The `radius_le_one_of_adj_all` lemma offers a direct path to proving a radius of at most 1, given certain conditions. The third lemma, `radius_le_one_of_romanWeight_le_two` appears to target a different, more specific set of constraints related to Roman dominating functions, which might prove useful later.\n\n\n**Applying radius-one lemma**\n\nAttempting to apply `radius_le_one_of_adj_all` by constructing the required adjacency condition. For arbitrary `w`, if `w` is not equal to `u`, a pair-sum inequality and the properties of `f` should show that `u` is adjacent to `w`. This requires using `hf w (f w = 0)`.\n\nTrying to derive that if `f w = 0`, then there exists `z` adjacent to `w`, and `f z = 2`. The fact that `z` must be `u` is derived by another pair-sum inequality. Now it can be concluded that u is adjacent to w.\n\n\n**Establishing subset inclusion**\n\nA subset relationship between the complement of the ball around *u* and the set of vertices with function value 1 is being proved.  Considered is an arbitrary vertex *v* outside the ball.  Showed that *v* cannot have a function value of 0 or 2, therefore it must have a function value of 1.\n\n**Bounding cardinalities via subset**\n\nThe cardinality of the complement is bounded by the cardinality of the filter based on the established subset. This requires proving the complement's cardinality can be derived in terms of the set.  Established the size of the complement.\n\n\n**Deriving cardinality bounds**\n\nConsidering the cardinality of the intersection of the closed ball around *u* and the universal set. Established that this equals the cardinality of the universal set. This implies the closed ball's cardinality is less than or equal to the total number of vertices.\n\nProved that the cardinality of the set of vertices with function value 1 equals the sum of their function values.  This uses the fact that the function value is always 1 for elements in that set.\n\nDerived an inequality relating the cardinality of the vertices with function value 1 plus 2 to the roman weight of the function. This involved considering the sum of function values over a related set.\n\n\n**Analyzing proof strategy**\n\nThe proof strategy seems to involve several case splits based on the relationship between the graph's cardinality and the Roman weight of the dominating function, and also the graph radius and Roman weight. The goal appears to be to show that the Roman domination number is bounded below. The intermediate results involve the radius and eccentricity.\n\n**Establishing radius bounds**\n\nIt appears several cases are being considered to establish bounds on the graph's radius. The cases are based on relationships to the Roman weight and the graph's size, aiming to prove results like `radius_add_one_le_romanWeight_of_card_le` or `radius_le_one_of_romanWeight_le_two`.\n\n**Exploring the no-two case**\n\nThe final case where the function value is never 2 is being considered. This will likely lead to some constraints on the function's weight. The previous cases likely eliminate edge conditions.\n\n**Considering intermediate bounds**\n\nThe code is deducing upper bounds for the graph's eccentricity using the roman weight function to derive the ultimate result.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":"{\"RequestFeedback\":false,\"Summary\":\"Draft full proof in test_full.lean to inspect the exact remaining subgoals.\",\"UserFacing\":false}","CodeContent":"\"import Mathlib\\nimport LeanProject.GraphInvariantsComputable\\n\\nset_option maxRecDepth 10000\\n\\nopen SimpleGraph\\n\\nabbrev Candidate : Prop :=\\n    ∀ {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj],\\n      GraphCalc.IsNontrivialClass G → GraphCalc.HasRadius G → GraphCalc.radius G + 1 ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G\\n\\nopen GraphCalc\\n\\nlemma minUpTo_le {n : ℕ} {p : ℕ → Prop} [DecidablePred p] (k : ℕ) (hk : k ≤ n) (hp : p k) :\\n    minUpTo n p ≤ k := by\\n  unfold minUpTo\\n  have hmem : k ∈ (Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p := by\\n    rw [Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_range]\\n    exact ⟨Nat.lt_succ_of_le hk, hp⟩\\n  have hmin := Finset.min_le hmem\\n  generalize hmin_eq : ((Finset.range (n + 1)).filter p).min = m\\n  rw [hmin_eq] at hmin\\n  cases m with\\n  | top => contradiction\\n  | coe val =>\\n    simp only [WithTop.coe_le_coe] at hmin\\n    exact hmin\\n\\ntheorem radius_le_eccentricity {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (v : V) :\\n    GraphCalc.radius G ≤ GraphCalc.eccentricity G v := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.radius\\n  have hmem : GraphCalc.eccentricity G v ∈ Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ := by\\n    apply Finset.mem_image_of_mem\\n    exact Finset.mem_univ v\\n  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Finset.min_of_mem hmem\\n  rw [hb]\\n  have hle : (Finset.image (GraphCalc.eccentricity G) Finset.univ).min ≤ ↑(GraphCalc.eccentricity G v) :=\\n    Finset.min_le hmem\\n  rw [hb] at hle\\n  exact WithTop.coe_le_coe.mp hle\\n\\nlemma le_romanDominationNumber {V : Type} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\\n    (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (k : ℕ)\\n    (h : ∀ f : V → Fin 3, GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f → k ≤ GraphCalc.romanWeight f) :\\n    k ≤ GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber G := by\\n  unfold GraphCalc.romanDominationNumber\\n  have h_ex : ∃ f : V → Fin 3, GraphCalc.IsRomanDominatingFunction G f := by\\n    use (fun _ => 2)\\n    intro v hv\\n    dsimp at hv\\n    have h_false : Fa\n<truncated 21276 bytes>","Description":"\"Update test_full.lean with the nearly complete proof\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9/test_full.lean\"","toolAction":"\"Writing file\"","toolSummary":"\"Update test_full.lean\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
